WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.688 --> 00:43.899
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:43.982 --> 00:45.567
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:49.571 --> 00:51.573
[♪ gentle music playing]

9
00:58.580 --> 00:59.706
-[Youjin] Boo! -You scared me.

10
01:00.332 --> 01:01.792
[Youjin] I got you.

11
01:01.875 --> 01:03.335
I was just messing with you.

12
01:11.301 --> 01:13.178
Sorry, I kept you waiting.

13
01:26.358 --> 01:28.527
I was just trying to pull a little prank on you.

14
01:32.114 --> 01:33.365
Did I scare you that badly?

15
01:35.826 --> 01:37.744
Are you mad?

16
01:40.914 --> 01:41.957
No.

17
01:43.166 --> 01:44.167
I just...

18
01:45.585 --> 01:47.087
hugged you because I like you.

19
01:48.964 --> 01:51.133
Because I like you so much.

20
02:02.352 --> 02:04.354
[video game beeping]

21
02:06.314 --> 02:09.818
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE 1

22
02:09.901 --> 02:12.320
[Youseong] Mom, is that fun?

23
02:13.029 --> 02:14.614
EPISODE 8

24
02:14.698 --> 02:16.324
I don't know. I'm just reading it.

25
02:16.825 --> 02:18.326
I felt like reading a book.

26
02:19.619 --> 02:20.620
Did you buy it?

27
02:21.705 --> 02:23.623
Of course. Would I find it on the street?

28
02:25.083 --> 02:27.085
I was bored, so I went to the bookstore,

29
02:27.169 --> 02:28.628
and this one looked interesting.

30
02:31.590 --> 02:34.634
Is it about how people are lonely or something?

31
02:38.638 --> 02:39.723
Are you lonely?

32
02:40.265 --> 02:42.309
Everyone is lonely.

33
02:45.187 --> 02:48.690
It doesn't matter if you have a husband or kids.

34
02:51.401 --> 02:54.905
Sometimes I wonder why my life is the way it is.

35
02:54.988 --> 02:56.698
It's sad and lonely.

36
03:00.035 --> 03:02.746
Your life is sad and lonely?

37
03:04.706 --> 03:06.124
I don't know.

38
03:06.208 --> 03:07.375
Maybe it's menopause.

39
03:08.168 --> 03:12.506
One minute I feel good, the next I feel awful.

40
03:13.089 --> 03:14.341
I'm hot, then cold.

41
03:14.424 --> 03:17.052
I laugh, then I cry. I'm all over the place. Jeez.

42
03:18.053 --> 03:20.347
I don't know. I'm old now.

43
03:20.430 --> 03:21.848
I'm old.

44
03:21.932 --> 03:23.225
It's not because you're old.

45
03:23.308 --> 03:24.976
It's all because of Lim Youjin.

46
03:26.353 --> 03:28.939
What's wrong with accepting some fruit from a customer?

47
03:29.022 --> 03:31.358
Who does she think she is to chew you out like that?

48
03:31.441 --> 03:33.610
Well, that was actually my fault.

49
03:34.569 --> 03:37.197
I should've known better than to make a mistake like that.

50
03:37.280 --> 03:38.532
Yeah, exactly.

51
03:38.615 --> 03:40.492
It was just a mistake. Right?

52
03:40.575 --> 03:43.954
That brat shouldn't cry and yell at her mom over that.

53
03:44.037 --> 03:45.997
She was probably upset herself.

54
03:47.290 --> 03:50.085
I don't even get what's so upsetting about it,

55
03:50.168 --> 03:53.088
let alone why she'd throw such a huge tantrum at you over it.

56
03:53.171 --> 03:55.840
Does she think she's so sophisticated and classy?

57
03:56.550 --> 03:58.760
At the end of the day, she's still your daughter.

58
04:01.972 --> 04:03.265
I can't seem to poop. [sighs]

59
04:04.140 --> 04:05.767
[Youseong] This is all because of you, Dad.

60
04:07.060 --> 04:08.061
[Yongseok] What is?

61
04:08.770 --> 04:13.358
If you'd bought Mom expensive fruit and broadened her horizons,

62
04:14.359 --> 04:16.611
she wouldn't be reading this stupid book now.

63
04:18.363 --> 04:19.698
What? What book?

64
04:20.365 --> 04:21.783
[Youseong] One Hundred Years of Solitude.

65
04:23.326 --> 04:25.787
Just talking about it is pissing me off all over again.

66
04:26.788 --> 04:27.914
Hey! Lim Youjin!

67
04:27.998 --> 04:29.124
Come on out.

68
04:29.875 --> 04:32.294
Your mom is feeling lonely because of you,

69
04:32.377 --> 04:34.379
and now she is reading this stupid book!

70
04:35.297 --> 04:36.798
Get out here, you little brat!

71
04:36.882 --> 04:37.924
Be quiet.

72
04:38.383 --> 04:40.302
Youjin isn't even in her room right now.

73
04:40.385 --> 04:41.386
She's out?

74
04:41.970 --> 04:43.889
I thought she was home. When did she leave?

75
04:43.972 --> 04:45.807
Yeah, she went to the grocery store.

76
04:45.891 --> 04:47.851
I asked her to get some tofu. [sighs]

77
04:49.811 --> 04:51.563
[Youjin] Are you sure nothing's up?

78
04:51.646 --> 04:53.106
[Minjae] Hmm?

79
04:53.189 --> 04:54.232
No. Nothing's up.

80
04:55.108 --> 04:56.109
[Youjin] Hmm.

81
04:56.902 --> 04:58.486
Nothing's up,

82
04:58.570 --> 05:00.989
but you suddenly wanted to see me?

83
05:01.072 --> 05:02.157
Out of nowhere?

84
05:03.241 --> 05:04.242
[Minjae] Yeah.

85
05:05.785 --> 05:06.912
[Youjin] You like me that much?

86
05:10.916 --> 05:12.334
What's so great about me?

87
05:15.837 --> 05:17.756
Tell me. What is it that you like so much?

88
05:19.633 --> 05:21.927
Just... everything.

89
05:22.677 --> 05:26.640
Mmm. No, you have to be specific. Be specific.

90
05:28.516 --> 05:29.809
[Minjae] Hmm...

91
05:31.186 --> 05:33.897
[sighs] You're taking way too long to answer.

92
05:37.734 --> 05:38.735
You're pretty.

93
05:40.111 --> 05:41.613
I'm pretty. What else?

94
05:41.696 --> 05:42.781
-What else? -Yeah.

95
05:44.824 --> 05:45.825
What else?

96
05:45.909 --> 05:46.910
You're cute.

97
05:47.577 --> 05:49.204
I'm pretty and cute.

98
05:49.287 --> 05:50.622
-What else? -What else?

99
05:51.706 --> 05:52.707
[Minjae] Hmm.

100
05:52.791 --> 05:53.959
You're nice.

101
05:54.793 --> 05:57.253
I'm pretty, cute, and nice.

102
05:57.337 --> 05:58.380
What else?

103
05:58.463 --> 05:59.464
[chuckles softly] More?

104
06:00.674 --> 06:02.550
Well, you only said three things.

105
06:02.634 --> 06:04.469
That I'm pretty, cute, and nice.

106
06:05.178 --> 06:06.638
Come on, keep going.

107
06:07.180 --> 06:08.723
Keep going? Just keep going?

108
06:08.807 --> 06:09.891
Yeah.

109
06:09.975 --> 06:12.519
Come on, I'm asking you to write a thesis, am I?

110
06:12.602 --> 06:15.105
You should have enough for two to three pages.

111
06:15.772 --> 06:16.773
Is that so hard?

112
06:17.691 --> 06:19.859
[Minjae] Hmm.

113
06:22.946 --> 06:24.030
Well... What about you?

114
06:24.114 --> 06:25.115
[Youjin] Hmm?

115
06:25.198 --> 06:28.118
I mean, there must be things you like about me too.

116
06:28.201 --> 06:30.829
Go ahead and fill two pages.

117
06:33.540 --> 06:34.958
[Youjin] Hmm...

118
06:38.044 --> 06:39.379
You're taking a while too.

119
06:43.008 --> 06:44.467
I can't say anything.

120
06:44.551 --> 06:46.177
Because I don't like you.

121
06:47.762 --> 06:48.763
Huh?

122
06:50.473 --> 06:51.474
What?

123
06:54.269 --> 06:55.937
What are you talking about?

124
06:56.604 --> 06:57.731
You said you liked me.

125
06:58.690 --> 06:59.691
When did I say that?

126
07:00.650 --> 07:03.987
You said you liked me before.

127
07:06.906 --> 07:09.200
When did I say I liked you?

128
07:09.284 --> 07:10.493
I said I loved you.

129
07:12.787 --> 07:16.166
[Youjin giggling]

130
07:18.209 --> 07:19.210
I love you.

131
07:20.295 --> 07:21.296
Me too.

132
07:25.258 --> 07:26.301
Hey...

133
07:27.677 --> 07:30.138
Hey, we're in public. Don't.

134
07:30.221 --> 07:32.807
What? You've never kissed in public before?

135
07:33.975 --> 07:35.351
[softly] Come on, don't.

136
07:35.435 --> 07:38.229
-Are you embarrassed? Your ears are red. -Come on, stop it.

137
07:38.313 --> 07:39.314
Why?

138
07:39.397 --> 07:40.607
Stop it.

139
07:40.690 --> 07:42.650
Come on, what if someone sees us? [chuckles awkwardly] Stop.

140
07:44.903 --> 07:47.280
Wait, are you mad?

141
07:47.906 --> 07:49.491
You're even cuter when you're mad.

142
07:50.658 --> 07:52.452
Don't say I'm cute. I'm older than you.

143
07:52.535 --> 07:54.537
[Youjin chuckling]

144
07:54.621 --> 07:55.997
You're so cute.

145
07:56.080 --> 07:57.749
You're so cute, I want to bite you.

146
07:57.832 --> 07:58.833
Nom!

147
07:58.917 --> 08:00.168
Don't bite. Don't bite me.

148
08:00.251 --> 08:01.586
-I want to. -Don't bite me.

149
08:01.669 --> 08:03.546
-I want to bite you. -It'll hurt. Stop it.

150
08:03.630 --> 08:05.173
-Come on, come here. -Stop it.

151
08:05.256 --> 08:06.508
Nobody's watching.

152
08:06.591 --> 08:08.259
-[cellphone vibrating] -You're getting a call. Answer it.

153
08:09.010 --> 08:10.178
What? Who's calling me?

154
08:11.721 --> 08:12.722
Mom?

155
08:13.973 --> 08:14.974
I'll be quiet.

156
08:16.476 --> 08:17.894
Mom. What's up?

157
08:19.521 --> 08:20.522
Tofu?

158
08:21.981 --> 08:23.274
Ah...

159
08:23.358 --> 08:24.734
The convenience store was out,

160
08:24.818 --> 08:26.903
so I came to the supermarket on the main road.

161
08:26.986 --> 08:28.988
You could've just come back if they were out.

162
08:29.072 --> 08:30.490
You didn't have to go that far.

163
08:32.575 --> 08:34.661
Well, I was wondering

164
08:34.744 --> 08:37.539
why it was taking you so long just to get some tofu.

165
08:37.622 --> 08:38.832
Yeah.

166
08:38.915 --> 08:39.999
I sent Youseong over.

167
08:40.083 --> 08:41.125
You haven't seen him?

168
08:41.209 --> 08:42.293
Youseong?

169
08:43.670 --> 08:45.797
I haven't seen him.

170
08:47.048 --> 08:48.091
Yeah.

171
08:48.675 --> 08:49.676
Oh...

172
08:50.927 --> 08:52.303
I bought the tofu.

173
08:52.387 --> 08:53.388
Yeah.

174
08:54.013 --> 08:56.683
Uh... I'm nearby. I'll be home soon.

175
08:56.766 --> 08:57.809
I'm on my way now.

176
08:58.768 --> 09:00.103
Yeah, in the alley.

177
09:00.979 --> 09:02.897
Well, in like two to three minutes?

178
09:04.566 --> 09:05.900
-[Minjae mouthing] Are you leaving? Okay. -Yeah.

179
09:06.526 --> 09:07.527
[Minjae mouthing] Go. Go ahead.

180
09:08.278 --> 09:09.696
-[door bell chimes] -[Youjin] Yeah.

181
09:09.779 --> 09:10.989
I already bought it.

182
09:11.656 --> 09:13.700
-[door bell chimes] -[Youjin speaking indistinctly]

183
09:13.783 --> 09:15.785
[♪ slow pop music playing over speakers]

184
09:43.938 --> 09:45.940
[♪ music stops]

185
09:50.904 --> 09:53.198
[Youseong] We've met at school before, right?

186
09:54.365 --> 09:55.366
Yes.

187
09:56.492 --> 09:58.161
[Youseong] What brings you to our neighborhood?

188
09:59.871 --> 10:01.539
I was just...

189
10:01.623 --> 10:02.916
[Youseong] Are you here to meet Youjin?

190
10:06.461 --> 10:07.545
Yes.

191
10:09.005 --> 10:10.882
So, what's your relationship with Youjin?

192
10:11.841 --> 10:12.842
Boyfriend?

193
10:13.593 --> 10:14.594
[Minjae] Pardon?

194
10:15.720 --> 10:17.430
Are you two dating?

195
10:19.432 --> 10:20.892
Yes, we're dating.

196
10:20.975 --> 10:22.977
-We're serious about our relationship. -[Youseong sighs]

197
10:23.895 --> 10:25.563
[tuts] Serious?

198
10:26.272 --> 10:30.401
[Minjae] We're seriously and genuinely dating.

199
10:30.485 --> 10:31.486
Since when?

200
10:31.569 --> 10:35.990
Well, we first met last fall.

201
10:36.074 --> 10:38.409
But we parted ways without even exchanging names.

202
10:38.993 --> 10:40.828
Then we met again this year...

203
10:40.912 --> 10:42.538
[Youseong] So you've been together since then?

204
10:43.039 --> 10:44.707
No, not really.

205
10:45.667 --> 10:47.669
We only started officially dating recently.

206
10:47.752 --> 10:50.171
So if you only just started dating,

207
10:50.255 --> 10:52.340
I guess you two haven't gotten that far yet.

208
10:54.842 --> 10:55.843
Pardon?

209
10:55.927 --> 10:57.762
Come on, quit playing dumb.

210
10:59.055 --> 11:01.891
Did you mess around with my sister or not, you little punk?

211
11:04.435 --> 11:05.478
Gosh, seriously.

212
11:07.355 --> 11:09.732
[sighs heavily, smacks lips]

213
11:09.816 --> 11:13.778
First off, our family is extremely conservative and strict.

214
11:13.861 --> 11:15.446
It's basically the Joseon dynasty.

215
11:17.782 --> 11:18.783
Oh...

216
11:18.866 --> 11:22.120
So even if you two are dating, don't cross any lines, okay?

217
11:22.662 --> 11:24.914
Keep it wholesome and innocent.

218
11:29.043 --> 11:30.962
You can look at her, but don't touch.

219
11:33.798 --> 11:35.216
Aren't you going to answer me?

220
11:35.300 --> 11:37.510
Yeah, sure. I understand. Yeah.

221
11:38.094 --> 11:40.305
And don't stay out too late, okay?

222
11:40.388 --> 11:43.558
When the clock hits 10 p.m., you bring her straight home.

223
11:46.060 --> 11:47.061
Okay.

224
11:48.563 --> 11:50.106
So does that mean you approve?

225
11:50.189 --> 11:52.108
You're okay with me dating Youjin?

226
11:52.191 --> 11:53.860
Well, I'm not her mom or dad.

227
11:53.943 --> 11:55.862
It's not my place to approve or disapprove.

228
11:56.362 --> 11:58.656
I'm just laying down some ground rules.

229
11:59.282 --> 12:00.658
[Minjae] Okay. I understand.

230
12:03.202 --> 12:04.203
[sighs]

231
12:07.123 --> 12:10.209
By the way, I have a question.

232
12:10.293 --> 12:12.545
Sure, go ahead. You can ask me anything.

233
12:14.255 --> 12:16.215
I heard you had trouble with your leg,

234
12:17.467 --> 12:18.801
but it looks fine.

235
12:20.553 --> 12:23.681
Was it from a car accident or something?

236
12:23.765 --> 12:26.184
Oh, it wasn't a car accident.

237
12:26.267 --> 12:29.812
I had surgery because I had osteosarcoma.

238
12:29.896 --> 12:31.189
Osteosarcoma?

239
12:31.272 --> 12:32.774
What kind of disease is that?

240
12:33.358 --> 12:36.152
It's a tumor that develops in the bone or around a joint.

241
12:37.153 --> 12:38.154
So...

242
12:38.988 --> 12:41.532
I had part of it amputated.

243
12:42.950 --> 12:43.951
What?

244
12:45.787 --> 12:48.706
Wait, by "amputated," you mean...

245
12:49.665 --> 12:52.418
They cut off your leg?

246
12:54.754 --> 12:56.839
But your leg...

247
12:56.923 --> 13:01.010
Uh... I'm missing my right leg below the knee.

248
13:01.094 --> 13:03.721
I use a prosthetic leg to get around.

249
13:05.181 --> 13:06.516
Oh...

250
13:07.392 --> 13:09.602
Oh... I get it.

251
13:11.979 --> 13:13.022
I'm sorry.

252
13:13.106 --> 13:15.483
[Youseong] No, you have nothing to be sorry about.

253
13:17.151 --> 13:19.612
-You... -[Minjae] I'm just sorry.

254
13:20.154 --> 13:23.157
No, it's nothing to apologize for, but...

255
13:24.200 --> 13:25.618
I'm sorry.

256
13:34.544 --> 13:35.586
[Youseong] Mmm.

257
13:37.713 --> 13:40.049
We're almost done eating, and he's still not back.

258
13:40.675 --> 13:41.968
I know.

259
13:42.051 --> 13:44.804
They all go missing whenever they go out to buy tofu.

260
13:46.305 --> 13:47.557
Call him.

261
13:48.057 --> 13:51.018
Tell him he doesn't need to look for tofu. Tell him to come back.

262
13:51.519 --> 13:52.937
Did he take his phone with him?

263
13:53.020 --> 13:54.897
Yeah, I saw him take it with him earlier.

264
14:02.864 --> 14:03.990
Right, the tofu.

265
14:04.490 --> 14:06.409
[groans] I left it there.

266
14:06.492 --> 14:07.702
[cellphone vibrating]

267
14:11.372 --> 14:12.415
Hello?

268
14:12.498 --> 14:13.499
Where are you?

269
14:14.292 --> 14:17.170
Uh... Hurry back home. We're already done eating.

270
14:18.045 --> 14:20.089
-[Miyoung sighs in relief] -The tofu?

271
14:20.173 --> 14:21.340
You lost it?

272
14:22.091 --> 14:23.342
[Miyoung] What? He lost the tofu?

273
14:24.135 --> 14:25.344
That darn tofu.

274
14:26.262 --> 14:28.598
Tell him to just forget about it and come back.

275
14:29.223 --> 14:32.018
Hey, Dad says to forget about it and just hurry back.

276
14:33.728 --> 14:35.897
Just forget it and come home, okay?

277
14:38.024 --> 14:39.317
Hello?

278
14:39.400 --> 14:40.818
Lim Youseong, are you there?

279
14:41.736 --> 14:42.820
Hello?

280
14:43.863 --> 14:46.365
What... Are you there or did you hang up?

281
14:46.449 --> 14:47.700
I'm still here.

282
14:49.035 --> 14:50.870
Fine. I'll be there soon.

283
15:06.219 --> 15:08.221
[♪ pop music playing over speakers]

284
15:11.682 --> 15:12.850
[door bell chimes]

285
15:16.896 --> 15:18.773
-You're still here. -Uh...

286
15:18.856 --> 15:20.191
I was about to leave.

287
15:20.775 --> 15:22.193
I left that here, so...

288
15:22.276 --> 15:24.362
Yeah. Here. The tofu.

289
15:31.827 --> 15:33.496
[door bell chimes]

290
15:54.934 --> 15:58.020
No matter how I look at it, I just don't think this is okay.

291
15:58.980 --> 15:59.981
[Minjae] Sorry?

292
16:02.650 --> 16:04.110
Please stop seeing Youjin.

293
16:09.156 --> 16:11.492
It's easy to say it's discrimination or prejudice

294
16:12.576 --> 16:14.370
when it's not about you.

295
16:15.246 --> 16:18.249
[sighs] But now that it's my own sister,

296
16:19.250 --> 16:20.626
I just can't get past it.

297
16:22.753 --> 16:25.881
Please stop seeing my sister.

298
16:31.679 --> 16:35.933
But that's not something you can decide.

299
16:36.976 --> 16:37.977
What?

300
16:38.060 --> 16:40.938
And it's not something I can decide either.

301
16:41.522 --> 16:43.566
Youjin isn't a kid.

302
16:43.649 --> 16:44.859
She's an adult.

303
16:46.527 --> 16:49.071
She made the decision for herself,

304
16:49.155 --> 16:51.741
and no one has the right to interfere.

305
16:51.824 --> 16:52.825
Hmm...

306
16:54.243 --> 16:55.870
She's not a kid, she's an adult?

307
16:56.746 --> 16:57.788
Then what about you?

308
16:59.290 --> 17:01.250
You're even more of an adult than she is.

309
17:02.168 --> 17:05.379
You're more of an adult, so act like one.

310
17:07.131 --> 17:09.175
If some naive girl says she likes you,

311
17:09.258 --> 17:11.427
you don't just go, "Yay, I hit the jackpot!"

312
17:12.261 --> 17:13.554
You tell her no

313
17:14.388 --> 17:16.057
and to find someone better.

314
17:16.140 --> 17:18.851
That's what an adult would do. Am I wrong?

315
17:18.934 --> 17:19.935
[chuckles softly]

316
17:21.854 --> 17:24.231
Firstly, Youjin isn't some jackpot. She's a person.

317
17:24.315 --> 17:25.566
[Youseong] Don't get hung up on words.

318
17:25.649 --> 17:27.568
Why do you keep speaking informally to me?

319
17:27.651 --> 17:29.779
What if I am?

320
17:29.862 --> 17:33.824
You think I'm in any mood to be polite in a situation like this, sir?

321
17:37.703 --> 17:39.830
-If you're done, I'm leaving. -Wait.

322
17:41.290 --> 17:42.917
Do you really like Youjin?

323
17:47.963 --> 17:50.424
Yes, I really do.

324
17:51.967 --> 17:54.261
I genuinely like her a lot.

325
17:54.970 --> 17:57.431
If you like her, you should let her go.

326
17:58.265 --> 17:59.433
You know what they say.

327
17:59.517 --> 18:02.561
"If you love someone, set them free."

328
18:02.645 --> 18:05.398
You really are selfish, you know.

329
18:06.565 --> 18:07.566
[Youseong sighs]

330
18:09.360 --> 18:11.696
So you're saying you really can't break up with her?

331
18:12.154 --> 18:16.367
[scoffs] Well, as I said, that's not something I can decide.

332
18:16.450 --> 18:18.744
Well, stop putting it all on her.

333
18:18.828 --> 18:20.037
I'm not putting it on her.

334
18:20.121 --> 18:23.708
I can't go into every little detail with you right now,

335
18:23.791 --> 18:27.128
but Youjin cares about me so much,

336
18:27.211 --> 18:29.255
and she's put so much into this relationship.

337
18:30.172 --> 18:33.384
After all the love and effort she's given me,

338
18:33.467 --> 18:37.722
I owe it to her to give this everything I've got.

339
18:38.931 --> 18:43.310
Unless her feelings for me change or she falls for someone else,

340
18:43.394 --> 18:45.146
I may give up on other things,

341
18:47.064 --> 18:49.191
but I'll never give up on Youjin.

342
18:49.275 --> 18:51.902
[♪ emotional music playing]

343
18:59.660 --> 19:01.662
[keyboard clacking]

344
19:50.503 --> 19:52.588
WANT TO LEARN HOW TO PLAY POKER?

345
19:52.671 --> 19:54.173
JUST WATCH THIS!

346
19:54.840 --> 19:55.841
All right, everyone.

347
19:55.925 --> 19:58.260
Here are three tips for playing poker.

348
19:58.344 --> 20:02.681
First, remember your cards and your opponent's.

349
20:02.765 --> 20:07.686
And second, keep a close eye on your opponent.

350
20:07.770 --> 20:11.982
You want to watch for signs like darting eyes,

351
20:12.066 --> 20:16.195
stiff posture, or trembling hands.

352
20:16.278 --> 20:19.365
Then you can catch them bluffing.

353
20:20.074 --> 20:21.784
And third...

354
20:43.681 --> 20:45.015
[inhales sharply]

355
20:45.099 --> 20:47.101
[♪ quirky music builds]

356
20:55.317 --> 20:57.152
Would you like to bet?

357
20:57.236 --> 20:59.238
[♪ quirky music playing]

358
21:00.364 --> 21:01.365
[Chansoo] Half the pot.

359
21:03.826 --> 21:07.371
Five, four, three, two...

360
21:07.454 --> 21:08.455
[Hangyeol] Call.

361
21:09.623 --> 21:10.624
Call.

362
21:22.845 --> 21:24.388
Would you like to bet?

363
21:25.598 --> 21:29.643
-Five, four, three, two... -[Hangyeol sighs heavily]

364
21:35.190 --> 21:36.191
Fold.

365
21:39.695 --> 21:40.779
[Chansoo] You're such a coward.

366
21:42.197 --> 21:43.908
I'm not a coward.

367
21:43.991 --> 21:45.701
I just had a bad hand.

368
21:45.826 --> 21:49.872
So think it through before you fold.

369
21:49.955 --> 21:52.374
Well, I keep getting lousy hands.

370
21:52.458 --> 21:53.876
What am I supposed to do?

371
21:53.959 --> 21:54.960
All in.

372
21:58.422 --> 21:59.798
Don't look away.

373
21:59.882 --> 22:02.635
Keep your eyes right here.

374
22:04.929 --> 22:06.722
If you're scared, you can fold.

375
22:14.104 --> 22:15.689
[Minjae] Are you serious right now?

376
22:16.982 --> 22:18.400
What the hell are you doing?

377
22:19.360 --> 22:21.820
You're gambling at school? Seriously?

378
22:22.404 --> 22:24.239
We're not gambling.

379
22:24.740 --> 22:26.992
We're just having a little fun on our lunch break.

380
22:27.076 --> 22:28.118
What's the big deal?

381
22:28.786 --> 22:29.912
[Chansoo] We're not betting money.

382
22:29.995 --> 22:31.080
We're betting candy.

383
22:31.163 --> 22:32.289
I don't care what it is.

384
22:32.373 --> 22:34.625
Who said you could bring this stuff to school?

385
22:38.170 --> 22:39.797
A needle thief becomes an ox thief.

386
22:39.880 --> 22:42.508
You don't notice your clothes getting wet in a drizzle.

387
22:43.092 --> 22:45.177
Once you get hooked on this stuff,

388
22:45.260 --> 22:47.429
it'll ruin your life and tear your family apart.

389
22:47.513 --> 22:50.015
Don't you know how dangerous gambling addiction is?

390
22:50.099 --> 22:52.267
[mumbling] You don't even have a family...

391
22:52.351 --> 22:53.352
[Minjae tuts]

392
22:54.228 --> 22:56.188
[chuckling nervously] Sorry.

393
22:58.357 --> 22:59.608
I'm really sorry.

394
22:59.692 --> 23:02.903
I mean, this... This would get you in serious trouble anywhere.

395
23:02.987 --> 23:04.905
And you actually brought it to school?

396
23:05.781 --> 23:06.782
Who brought this?

397
23:07.408 --> 23:08.409
Who was it?

398
23:09.118 --> 23:11.161
[Hangyeol] Why did Sejin have to bring this...

399
23:12.413 --> 23:13.414
Was it you?

400
23:15.708 --> 23:16.750
I'm sorry.

401
23:17.251 --> 23:19.920
You get a few compliments, and now you can do whatever?

402
23:20.004 --> 23:21.005
No. I'm sorry.

403
23:24.008 --> 23:25.009
Throw it all out.

404
23:26.093 --> 23:27.594
-Okay. -Get rid of it. Now.

405
23:32.599 --> 23:34.101
[Taeho] Never bring this here again.

406
23:41.191 --> 23:42.192
[Hangyeol grunts]

407
23:46.572 --> 23:49.992
Hey, where did Lim Youjin go again, leaving her seat empty?

408
23:50.075 --> 23:52.494
Right, Youjin said she needed to study at the library,

409
23:52.578 --> 23:53.954
so I told her she could go.

410
23:55.706 --> 23:56.707
Oh...

411
23:56.790 --> 23:58.459
Youjin is the most sensible one here.

412
23:58.542 --> 24:00.544
[♪ stealthy music playing]

413
24:02.588 --> 24:03.589
[Youjin] Professor.

414
24:04.298 --> 24:05.299
Yes?

415
24:05.966 --> 24:07.968
Our genius Professor Talking Hat.

416
24:09.887 --> 24:11.263
Do you know how to play poker?

417
24:12.264 --> 24:13.265
No.

418
24:14.099 --> 24:15.934
[Youjin] Come on, you know how. Teach me.

419
24:17.853 --> 24:21.190
Poker takes both strategy and luck.

420
24:21.982 --> 24:24.526
But actually, it's just a simple game of probability.

421
24:25.360 --> 24:28.572
If you can do basic math,

422
24:28.655 --> 24:31.033
even an elementary school kid can pick it up.

423
24:31.116 --> 24:33.452
What are the odds of drawing an ace first?

424
24:35.204 --> 24:36.455
1 in 13.

425
24:39.374 --> 24:40.417
7.7%.

426
24:40.501 --> 24:41.627
7.7.

427
24:44.171 --> 24:45.714
If your first card is an ace,

428
24:45.798 --> 24:49.468
that leaves only three aces among the remaining 51 cards.

429
24:49.551 --> 24:54.598
The odds of drawing another ace are 3 in 51...

430
24:56.558 --> 24:57.810
which is 5.9%.

431
24:57.893 --> 24:59.561
Right. 5.9%.

432
24:59.645 --> 25:03.065
That's much lower than your chance of getting that first ace.

433
25:12.241 --> 25:13.242
[stutters]

434
25:14.118 --> 25:16.286
What... how did you do that?

435
25:16.370 --> 25:18.872
You have to remember every card to do this.

436
25:18.956 --> 25:19.957
You have to be smart.

437
25:21.083 --> 25:22.126
Wow.

438
25:23.377 --> 25:25.504
I'm saying you can't do it because you're dumb.

439
25:27.047 --> 25:30.008
Well, there are plenty of other poker techniques too,

440
25:30.092 --> 25:31.552
but when it comes down to it,

441
25:32.719 --> 25:35.973
the key skill is assessing the situation to make the right decision,

442
25:36.056 --> 25:39.351
maximizing your chances of making the best possible hand

443
25:39.434 --> 25:43.605
while calculating your opponent's odds, predicting what they're holding,

444
25:43.689 --> 25:46.316
and adjusting your strategy accordingly.

445
25:47.651 --> 25:48.652
Oh.

446
25:50.445 --> 25:52.865
[hesitates] There must be a foolproof system.

447
25:52.948 --> 25:54.408
Like a cheat sheet or something?

448
25:55.659 --> 25:57.494
You know, I've seen that in movies.

449
25:57.578 --> 26:00.080
Calculating the odds with an algorithm, like a computer.

450
26:00.164 --> 26:01.999
Yeah, I made one in elementary school.

451
26:02.875 --> 26:04.209
In elementary school?

452
26:04.751 --> 26:06.170
I got bored, so I made one.

453
26:08.755 --> 26:11.300
Then... could I have it?

454
26:12.634 --> 26:15.220
Think of it as saving my life, and give it to me. Please?

455
26:16.889 --> 26:18.307
And what will you do in return?

456
26:19.141 --> 26:20.142
What?

457
26:20.225 --> 26:23.645
That's three times I've saved you. And you expect me to do it for free?

458
26:24.354 --> 26:25.564
Do you have no shame?

459
26:27.024 --> 26:29.401
Uh... Well, what do you want me to do?

460
26:30.235 --> 26:32.112
Mmm... First,

461
26:32.946 --> 26:34.364
bow to me three times.

462
26:35.324 --> 26:36.575
-Bow? -[Jihoon] Yeah.

463
26:36.658 --> 26:38.619
Bow three times, and be my slave forever.

464
26:39.411 --> 26:40.537
Be your slave forever?

465
26:40.621 --> 26:43.665
Okay. I was kidding about the forever part. Just 30 years.

466
26:46.919 --> 26:47.920
Three years?

467
26:48.003 --> 26:49.213
No, I can't do that.

468
26:49.296 --> 26:50.297
It's too long.

469
26:51.006 --> 26:52.674
We're not done. Where are you going?

470
26:52.758 --> 26:54.468
I have a class. You should go too.

471
26:58.805 --> 26:59.806
Aren't you going?

472
27:01.433 --> 27:04.311
Professor, you're just kidding about making me your slave.

473
27:05.103 --> 27:06.897
I told you, I'm not going into math.

474
27:06.980 --> 27:09.650
I hate memorizing formulas, and proofs are hard.

475
27:10.192 --> 27:12.027
Everyone in the department is a genius.

476
27:12.110 --> 27:14.112
I know I wouldn't have any fun there.

477
27:14.196 --> 27:15.822
I'd just have a hard time.

478
27:19.826 --> 27:21.245
Then how about three months?

479
27:22.120 --> 27:24.498
Just one semester, until we hire a new TA.

480
27:24.581 --> 27:27.042
Just answer the phone and run some errands. That's it.

481
27:30.045 --> 27:31.213
[muttering] 560.

482
27:32.547 --> 27:35.133
224,848.

483
27:36.134 --> 27:39.721
Equals 1 over 595.

484
27:40.347 --> 27:46.103
The answer is 0.16807%.

485
27:46.186 --> 27:48.313
[♪ pensive music playing]

486
27:48.397 --> 27:50.148
There. Does that make sense?

487
27:51.566 --> 27:52.567
Well...

488
27:53.110 --> 27:55.028
If you don't get it, just memorize it.

489
27:56.697 --> 27:59.324
Uh... Theoretical probabilities rarely match

490
27:59.408 --> 28:01.660
what you actually observe in practice.

491
28:01.743 --> 28:03.787
Or every mathematician or probability expert

492
28:03.870 --> 28:05.372
would be getting rich at casinos.

493
28:07.165 --> 28:10.544
The outcome of a game of chance is also affected by the number of trials.

494
28:11.920 --> 28:14.381
Maybe that's what they call luck in this game.

495
28:14.464 --> 28:15.757
Anything else besides luck?

496
28:18.427 --> 28:19.469
Mind games?

497
28:20.429 --> 28:21.430
Mind games?

498
28:28.812 --> 28:33.358
I just sent you the revised slides and the updated graph.

499
28:34.317 --> 28:35.402
Okay, I'll take a look.

500
28:36.778 --> 28:38.780
[mouse clicking]

501
28:40.657 --> 28:42.534
Well done. You can go home now.

502
28:42.617 --> 28:44.161
Okay. I'll get going.

503
28:44.244 --> 28:45.245
[Minjae] Okay.

504
28:58.592 --> 28:59.593
Minjae,

505
29:00.510 --> 29:04.765
I'm sorry for all the trouble I caused today.

506
29:04.848 --> 29:05.849
Okay.

507
29:08.769 --> 29:12.689
Hey, never bring that stuff to school again.

508
29:19.571 --> 29:23.200
The two kinds of people I hate most are gamblers

509
29:25.368 --> 29:28.914
and people who make no effort and leave everything to luck.

510
29:29.790 --> 29:30.791
Okay.

511
29:30.874 --> 29:33.001
You see, I've got such high hopes for you.

512
29:33.085 --> 29:34.711
Don't let me down.

513
29:36.296 --> 29:37.923
Okay, got it.

514
29:41.802 --> 29:42.803
[Sejin sighs]

515
29:44.971 --> 29:46.848
By the way,

516
29:46.932 --> 29:48.975
who's giving the presentation for KEIT?

517
29:49.643 --> 29:51.770
Once you leave, there won't be anyone to do it.

518
29:51.853 --> 29:52.854
Is Taeho doing it?

519
29:54.106 --> 29:56.983
A junior shouldn't handle it when we have senior members, right?

520
29:59.236 --> 30:00.320
That...

521
30:01.905 --> 30:04.616
Well, it's not about being a junior member.

522
30:04.699 --> 30:05.992
I'm not going to the States.

523
30:06.076 --> 30:07.077
What?

524
30:07.160 --> 30:09.955
But you said you were doing your postdoc in the States.

525
30:10.455 --> 30:14.334
Well, I can do my postdoc anywhere and, mmm...

526
30:15.418 --> 30:17.420
Anyway, I'm not going. I'm staying here.

527
30:17.504 --> 30:19.673
But the professor said it's a great opportunity.

528
30:19.756 --> 30:20.924
Why aren't you going?

529
30:21.007 --> 30:22.175
It's a great opportunity.

530
30:22.259 --> 30:23.885
That's just how things turned out.

531
30:24.761 --> 30:25.887
Yeah.

532
30:25.971 --> 30:27.055
[door opens]

533
30:27.139 --> 30:28.515
[Youjin] I'm back.

534
30:32.894 --> 30:33.895
[whispering] Go.

535
30:36.982 --> 30:39.109
[Sejin] Library? You seem busy.

536
30:39.693 --> 30:41.903
Yeah. I was reading papers on torque sensors.

537
30:42.612 --> 30:44.281
I'll send my review by tomorrow.

538
30:44.364 --> 30:45.574
Okay. Thanks.

539
30:46.366 --> 30:47.367
[door opens]

540
30:48.118 --> 30:49.119
[door closes]

541
30:52.080 --> 30:53.623
Do you want to grab dinner?

542
30:53.707 --> 30:55.542
I have something to tell you too.

543
30:56.960 --> 30:59.713
Uh, I'm supposed to see a movie with Subin.

544
31:00.380 --> 31:01.590
Is it important?

545
31:02.299 --> 31:04.009
No, not really.

546
31:05.510 --> 31:07.679
Ah... Then let's do it another day.

547
31:07.762 --> 31:09.598
Tomorrow? Or the day after.

548
31:09.681 --> 31:10.891
Any day works for me.

549
31:11.641 --> 31:13.852
We could do that. Sure. Okay.

550
31:15.562 --> 31:18.148
I'm late. Sorry, but I have to head out. I'll call you.

551
31:18.231 --> 31:19.900
[Minjae] Okay, I'll call you later.

552
31:19.983 --> 31:21.985
Actually, why don't you call me when you...

553
31:22.903 --> 31:24.279
-head home? -[door closes]

554
31:45.759 --> 31:47.761
[♪ dramatic showdown music playing]

555
32:08.782 --> 32:10.784
[♪ music fades]

556
32:19.209 --> 32:20.210
[Sejin] Do you want beer?

557
32:20.293 --> 32:21.795
-[refrigerator door opens] -No.

558
32:22.295 --> 32:24.714
I don't want alcohol clouding my judgment.

559
32:25.215 --> 32:26.216
[Sejin scoffs]

560
32:31.930 --> 32:32.931
[grunts softly]

561
32:33.890 --> 32:35.892
[♪ slow tense music playing]

562
32:41.439 --> 32:45.819
Like I said, we're playing seven-card stud.

563
32:47.737 --> 32:52.450
Well, it's one hand only, so we're skipping the betting rounds.

564
32:53.368 --> 32:56.079
Half pot, double bet, minimum bet, quarter pot, full pot...

565
32:56.162 --> 32:57.580
We don't need any of that.

566
32:57.664 --> 32:59.499
No folding.

567
32:59.582 --> 33:03.086
We're going all in.

568
33:03.795 --> 33:05.797
[♪ music swells sharply with drum roll]

569
33:07.924 --> 33:09.926
[♪ music fades]

570
33:10.010 --> 33:11.011
Pick the cards.

571
33:11.511 --> 33:13.555
The dealer is supposed to pick the cards.

572
33:13.638 --> 33:14.681
I pick the cards?

573
33:14.764 --> 33:16.516
You're a player, not the dealer.

574
33:17.183 --> 33:19.311
What? So you're going to be the dealer?

575
33:19.394 --> 33:21.688
No, we need someone else.

576
33:33.992 --> 33:35.201
[Subin] Thank you.

577
33:46.629 --> 33:48.631
[♪ comical music playing]

578
34:00.435 --> 34:01.895
[Subin] Unit 301.

579
34:04.647 --> 34:06.649
-[doorbell chiming] -[♪ comical music continues playing]

580
34:10.695 --> 34:11.905
-[Youjin] Subin. You made it. -[Subin] Yeah.

581
34:11.988 --> 34:12.989
[Youjin] Come in, come in.

582
34:14.532 --> 34:15.533
What's that?

583
34:15.867 --> 34:17.952
[Subin] Huh? Ah...

584
34:18.036 --> 34:20.789
I heard you should bring a gift when you visit a new home.

585
34:21.956 --> 34:24.417
-You didn't need to. It's so heavy. -[Subin chuckles softly]

586
34:24.501 --> 34:25.502
Hello.

587
34:26.419 --> 34:27.545
Yes. Hello.

588
34:27.629 --> 34:28.630
What are you doing?

589
34:33.009 --> 34:34.010
[Youjin] Oh boy.

590
34:34.094 --> 34:35.470
-You can sit over there. -[Subin] Okay.

591
34:41.434 --> 34:43.228
[Youjin] Did you have trouble finding the place?

592
34:43.311 --> 34:44.521
No, I found it right away.

593
35:01.204 --> 35:02.205
CONTACTS

594
35:06.167 --> 35:08.169
CALLING... LIM YOUJIN

595
35:08.253 --> 35:09.421
[automation] The phone is turned off.

596
35:09.504 --> 35:11.297
-You will now be connected to voicemail... -[line disconnects]

597
35:12.507 --> 35:14.676
I thought she was going to the movies with her.

598
35:14.759 --> 35:15.844
What's going on now?

599
35:16.886 --> 35:17.887
Hmm?

600
35:21.266 --> 35:23.268
[♪ light comical music playing]

601
35:24.185 --> 35:25.770
Let's see.

602
35:46.249 --> 35:49.502
So the loser buys the winner a meal?

603
35:51.713 --> 35:54.424
-Yeah, so to speak. -[Subin] Hmm.

604
35:55.216 --> 35:58.428
-[Sejin chuckles awkwardly] -But I've never played poker.

605
35:59.429 --> 36:00.972
I don't know how to play.

606
36:01.055 --> 36:03.808
Ah... You're the dealer.

607
36:03.892 --> 36:05.894
Just hold on to the cards and then deal them.

608
36:05.977 --> 36:07.270
Oh.

609
36:08.062 --> 36:09.439
-Should I pick one? -[Youjin] Yes.

610
36:09.522 --> 36:10.523
[Subin] Okay.

611
36:10.607 --> 36:12.942
[♪ light zany music playing]

612
36:19.657 --> 36:21.159
-Should I shuffle the cards? -[Youjin] Yes.

613
36:26.080 --> 36:27.290
[smacks lips]

614
36:27.373 --> 36:30.752
Well, it's one hand only, so we're skipping the betting rounds.

615
36:30.835 --> 36:34.214
Half pot, double bet, minimum bet, quarter pot... We don't need any of that.

616
36:34.297 --> 36:36.049
No folding. We're going all in.

617
36:37.383 --> 36:38.968
What's half pot and double bet?

618
36:39.052 --> 36:41.805
Hmm? Ah... Those are just different bet sizes.

619
36:42.222 --> 36:43.890
[Subin] Oh. [chuckles softly]

620
36:43.973 --> 36:46.017
Sorry. I don't know much about poker.

621
36:46.100 --> 36:48.895
-[Sejin] No, it's okay. -[Subin chuckling]

622
36:54.108 --> 36:56.110
[♪ light mysterious music playing]

623
37:04.369 --> 37:06.621
-[line connects] -[automation] The phone is turned off.

624
37:06.704 --> 37:09.582
-You will now be connected to voicemail... -[line disconnects]

625
37:33.690 --> 37:35.775
[softly] Kim Sejin. Where are you?

626
37:37.151 --> 37:38.486
CONTACTS KIM SEJIN

627
37:38.570 --> 37:40.655
CALLING... KIM SEJIN

628
37:40.738 --> 37:42.156
[automation] The phone is turned off.

629
37:42.240 --> 37:44.033
You will now be connected to voicemail.

630
37:44.117 --> 37:45.910
You will be charged after the tone.

631
37:45.994 --> 37:47.829
-[beeps] -[line disconnects]

632
37:55.169 --> 37:57.922
Now, deal three cards to each of us, face down.

633
37:58.006 --> 37:59.007
[Subin] Okay.

634
38:00.049 --> 38:01.801
No, not like that. One at a time.

635
38:01.885 --> 38:02.886
One at a time.

636
38:05.555 --> 38:06.556
[Youjin] Yeah.

637
38:14.814 --> 38:15.982
[Subin] Mmm. [chuckles softly]

638
38:19.444 --> 38:21.362
Now, deal one card each, face up.

639
38:21.446 --> 38:22.447
-Face up? -[Youjin] Yeah.

640
38:23.072 --> 38:24.365
[Sejin] Oh.

641
38:24.449 --> 38:25.992
-Here. There you go. -[Subin] Mmm-hmm.

642
38:26.075 --> 38:29.537
[Sejin] Here.

643
38:30.496 --> 38:33.291
Here.

644
38:33.374 --> 38:35.919
And deal the last card to each player face down.

645
38:36.002 --> 38:37.003
Here.

646
38:38.296 --> 38:39.297
Here.

647
38:48.514 --> 38:49.599
[Youjin] Hmm.

648
38:49.682 --> 38:51.059
A royal flush?

649
38:51.851 --> 38:53.102
[♪ music peaks briefly]

650
38:53.186 --> 38:54.646
What? Are you scared?

651
38:54.729 --> 38:55.897
[snickering]

652
38:56.522 --> 38:58.816
A 0.003% chance.

653
39:00.568 --> 39:01.611
[sighing] Well...

654
39:02.612 --> 39:04.280
We don't want it to end too quickly.

655
39:04.364 --> 39:05.698
And it's only the first hand.

656
39:07.200 --> 39:08.826
How about we allow just one fold?

657
39:08.910 --> 39:10.370
But it'll cost you a slap. Deal?

658
39:11.037 --> 39:12.538
What? A slap?

659
39:12.622 --> 39:14.832
Well, I didn't mean an actual slap.

660
39:15.416 --> 39:17.126
-I was just joking. Just joking. -[Subin chuckles softly]

661
39:17.210 --> 39:19.003
-[Sejin chuckles] -Just joking.

662
39:19.087 --> 39:22.256
Is a royal flush a good thing?

663
39:23.091 --> 39:24.092
[Youjin sighing] Yes.

664
39:24.842 --> 39:27.136
It's the best hand. It beats everything.

665
39:27.679 --> 39:29.722
Wow.

666
39:30.848 --> 39:32.183
Can I see yours too?

667
39:32.266 --> 39:33.267
Well...

668
39:33.351 --> 39:35.520
[Youjin] Show her. She wants to see your cards.

669
39:35.603 --> 39:37.188
I want to see. Please show me.

670
39:41.109 --> 39:42.110
[Sejin sighing]

671
39:46.739 --> 39:47.740
[Subin] Hmm.

672
39:47.824 --> 39:50.451
If Kim Sejin has the ace of hearts,

673
39:50.535 --> 39:52.704
the royal flush is complete.

674
39:53.538 --> 39:54.747
Oh.

675
39:55.206 --> 39:56.541
-Does he have it? -You little...

676
39:57.166 --> 39:58.751
I can't tell you that.

677
39:58.835 --> 40:01.087
Lim Youjin, are you going to play dirty like this?

678
40:02.505 --> 40:05.633
[sighs] Kim Sejin, you don't have the ace.

679
40:06.050 --> 40:08.052
[♪ dramatic Western music playing]

680
40:08.761 --> 40:10.054
Because I've got three.

681
40:10.138 --> 40:11.347
It's a full house.

682
40:11.431 --> 40:12.432
[suppressed squeal] Yes!

683
40:15.268 --> 40:17.437
[chuckling] Yes!

684
40:19.105 --> 40:21.899
[sighing in relief]

685
40:21.983 --> 40:25.028
-[Sejin groans] -[doorbell chiming]

686
40:28.156 --> 40:30.324
-[Subin] Isn't that Minjae? -[Youjin shushes]

687
40:49.844 --> 40:51.846
[♪ light suspenseful music playing]

688
40:58.352 --> 41:00.855
What the... Those punks.

689
41:12.450 --> 41:13.826
[softly] But why do we have to hide?

690
41:15.244 --> 41:16.954
[whispering] I can't explain right now. Sorry.

691
41:17.455 --> 41:18.456
[whispering] I'm sorry.

692
41:18.539 --> 41:19.540
[whispering] It's okay.

693
41:20.625 --> 41:21.959
Hey, Kim Sejin.

694
41:22.043 --> 41:25.546
I won the game, so you're handing in your resignation at the lab next week

695
41:25.630 --> 41:27.090
and going back to Daejeon, okay?

696
41:27.173 --> 41:28.800
Are you serious, though?

697
41:28.883 --> 41:29.926
[Youjin] Yes, I am.

698
41:30.009 --> 41:31.302
That was the deal.

699
41:31.385 --> 41:33.513
He's going to quit the lab and leave?

700
41:33.596 --> 41:34.597
[Youjin] Yeah.

701
41:35.181 --> 41:37.725
He said he'd quit and leave if he lost the poker game.

702
41:38.309 --> 41:39.310
[Subin] No way.

703
41:39.393 --> 41:41.062
Who would bet that on a poker game?

704
41:41.145 --> 41:42.146
[Youjin] Exactly.

705
41:42.230 --> 41:44.023
It was his idea to do this bet.

706
41:44.107 --> 41:45.358
That's how crazy he is.

707
41:45.983 --> 41:48.361
Hey, don't go back on your word.

708
41:48.444 --> 41:49.695
You promised.

709
41:51.072 --> 41:52.365
-[doorbell chiming] -[Sejin grunts]

710
41:52.448 --> 41:53.449
Hey! [shushes]

711
41:53.533 --> 41:55.409
-[doorbell chiming] -[Sejin whispering] Turn it off.

712
41:55.868 --> 41:56.911
[knocking at door]

713
41:57.620 --> 41:59.622
[Minjae] Hey, I know you guys are in there.

714
42:00.164 --> 42:01.749
You better come open this door.

715
42:02.708 --> 42:05.419
If you don't open this door by the time I count to three,

716
42:05.503 --> 42:08.047
you guys are going to be in serious trouble. Huh?

717
42:11.092 --> 42:15.429
Three, two, one.

718
42:21.310 --> 42:23.354
[sighs, scoffs]

719
42:28.067 --> 42:30.069
[♪ light comical music playing]

720
42:38.327 --> 42:42.790
The three of you turned off the lights, locked the door, and were hiding.

721
42:45.084 --> 42:46.794
What were you three doing in here?

722
42:50.548 --> 42:51.799
Are you going to answer me?

723
42:57.180 --> 42:58.181
Jung Subin.

724
42:59.182 --> 43:00.183
[Subin] Yes.

725
43:00.516 --> 43:01.517
[Minjae] You tell me.

726
43:02.393 --> 43:04.395
You were supposed to see a movie with Youjin.

727
43:04.478 --> 43:05.605
What are you doing here?

728
43:13.154 --> 43:14.822
You guys were fighting again, right?

729
43:16.324 --> 43:18.910
Were you throwing punches? Pulling each other's hair?

730
43:18.993 --> 43:20.286
You had an MMA match?

731
43:20.369 --> 43:21.829
No, it's not like that.

732
43:22.830 --> 43:24.415
We were playing cards.

733
43:26.584 --> 43:27.668
Playing cards?

734
43:37.470 --> 43:39.180
You can play cards at home.

735
43:41.766 --> 43:43.100
But why did you hide?

736
43:43.184 --> 43:45.603
That, I'm not sure.

737
43:46.437 --> 43:48.147
Were you guys playing for money?

738
43:48.231 --> 43:49.899
No, we weren't playing for money.

739
43:51.525 --> 43:53.319
-It wasn't money, but... -[Minjae] Then what is it?

740
43:59.075 --> 44:00.952
If Sejin lost,

741
44:01.035 --> 44:03.788
he'd quit the lab and go back to Daejeon.

742
44:12.838 --> 44:14.340
Kim Sejin, Jung Subin, get up.

743
44:21.472 --> 44:24.642
But... I didn't initiate it.

744
44:24.725 --> 44:27.561
Uh... It was Kim Sejin's idea to play.

745
44:28.104 --> 44:29.105
She's right.

746
44:29.855 --> 44:32.483
Youjin didn't do anything wrong.

747
44:33.651 --> 44:36.320
This was all my fault, and I take full responsibility.

748
44:37.530 --> 44:41.617
[sighs heavily] I should've treated my only lab mate better, but I failed to.

749
44:42.159 --> 44:45.288
I guess that caused some misunderstandings, and here we are...

750
44:46.580 --> 44:49.000
I'll accept whatever punishment you give me.

751
44:49.083 --> 44:52.378
I'll take a good look at myself and reflect on what I've done.

752
44:52.461 --> 44:55.673
What, you're going to take a good look at yourself and reflect? You?

753
44:56.257 --> 44:57.258
Hey.

754
44:59.635 --> 45:03.014
If you want me to go to Daejeon, I will.

755
45:04.432 --> 45:07.184
If you want me to quit the lab, I will.

756
45:07.268 --> 45:09.770
I'll do whatever you say.

757
45:10.855 --> 45:12.106
Okay. Fine.

758
45:12.189 --> 45:13.607
[groaning] Oh, come on.

759
45:13.691 --> 45:16.277
Kim Sejin is just faking it to not go to Daejeon.

760
45:16.986 --> 45:19.113
Hey, you're real clever.

761
45:19.196 --> 45:20.364
You're so sneaky.

762
45:20.448 --> 45:22.491
Hey, did I say you could get up?

763
45:22.575 --> 45:25.411
Well, I didn't do anything wrong. Why do I have to kneel?

764
45:25.494 --> 45:27.079
You didn't do anything wrong?

765
45:27.621 --> 45:30.541
I didn't do anything wrong. Who are you to treat me like this?

766
45:30.624 --> 45:32.335
Even my parents wouldn't do this.

767
45:32.418 --> 45:34.587
Yeah? You're proud of what you've done?

768
45:34.670 --> 45:36.422
Is that why you're talking back to me?

769
45:37.006 --> 45:38.007
I'm just saying,

770
45:39.216 --> 45:41.761
Kim Sejin made the bet in the first place.

771
45:42.345 --> 45:44.055
If I won, he'd go back to Daejeon,

772
45:44.138 --> 45:46.390
and if he won, I'd have to break up with you.

773
45:48.351 --> 45:50.519
Playing poker was his idea, too.

774
45:50.603 --> 45:53.314
And now that I actually won, he's going back on his word.

775
45:57.234 --> 45:58.235
[Minjae] Hey, Lim Youjin.

776
46:00.654 --> 46:01.655
Come with me.

777
46:01.739 --> 46:03.741
[♪ emotional music playing]

778
46:09.663 --> 46:10.790
Hey, wait up.

779
46:42.154 --> 46:43.781
[door lock beeps]

780
46:44.698 --> 46:45.825
[door lock chimes]

781
47:13.185 --> 47:14.478
What are you doing?

782
47:15.855 --> 47:17.231
Why did you throw your jacket?

783
47:17.314 --> 47:18.732
I'm the one who should be mad.

784
47:19.483 --> 47:21.110
So you think what you did was okay?

785
47:22.111 --> 47:24.405
[sighs] How many times do I have to tell you?

786
47:24.488 --> 47:26.282
I told you, he started the fight.

787
47:27.491 --> 47:29.827
You just

788
47:30.494 --> 47:33.205
bet our relationship on a card game. Huh?

789
47:35.124 --> 47:38.377
I know you're young and immature, but how could you do that?

790
47:39.795 --> 47:41.088
If you had lost the game,

791
47:41.172 --> 47:43.299
were you actually going to break up with me?

792
47:43.924 --> 47:44.967
But I won.

793
47:45.050 --> 47:46.135
[Minjae chuckling] "But I won?"

794
47:46.635 --> 47:47.928
What if you had lost?

795
47:49.305 --> 47:50.473
I didn't lose.

796
47:50.556 --> 47:53.642
Even if I had, I wouldn't break up over this. Isn't that obvious?

797
47:53.726 --> 47:56.061
[loudly] I'm saying it's not obvious!

798
47:59.607 --> 48:01.484
All right. I'm sorry.

799
48:01.567 --> 48:02.651
[Minjae] All right?

800
48:03.527 --> 48:05.154
What's all right?

801
48:06.697 --> 48:07.698
You...

802
48:09.116 --> 48:12.495
Is everything just easy, just a joke to you?

803
48:13.245 --> 48:14.705
[Youjin] What are you saying?

804
48:14.788 --> 48:16.790
When did I say everything was a joke?

805
48:16.874 --> 48:19.877
You just bet our relationship on a game,

806
48:19.960 --> 48:22.630
like it's no big deal, like it's all just a joke!

807
48:22.713 --> 48:23.714
Am I wrong?

808
48:23.797 --> 48:26.050
You're the one who treats me like I'm no big deal.

809
48:26.884 --> 48:27.885
[Minjae] What?

810
48:28.469 --> 48:31.180
You made me kneel, yelled at me, and even threw your jacket.

811
48:32.056 --> 48:35.142
You treated me with zero respect just because I like you more.

812
48:35.226 --> 48:37.478
That's because you did something wrong.

813
48:37.978 --> 48:41.065
Even if I did, you don't treat someone you care about like that.

814
48:41.732 --> 48:43.692
Then don't give me a reason to be mad.

815
48:45.361 --> 48:46.487
[sighs]

816
48:46.570 --> 48:48.280
This is seriously messed up.

817
48:49.782 --> 48:51.742
I chose someone who doesn't love me back,

818
48:51.825 --> 48:53.452
so I can somehow live with that.

819
48:54.912 --> 48:57.289
Being falsely blamed and misunderstood really sucks.

820
49:00.125 --> 49:01.418
I guess I lost after all.

821
49:02.711 --> 49:03.712
What?

822
49:05.464 --> 49:07.091
What do you mean, you lost?

823
49:07.174 --> 49:08.300
-Hey. -[Youjin] I'm going to go.

824
49:08.384 --> 49:09.385
[Minjae] Hey!

825
49:12.972 --> 49:14.974
[♪ melancholic music playing]

826
49:17.476 --> 49:18.686
Hey, let me take you home.

827
49:18.769 --> 49:20.020
I can get home by myself.

828
49:20.104 --> 49:21.855
I'll take you home. What's wrong?

829
49:21.939 --> 49:22.940
[Youjin] I said I'm okay.

830
49:24.858 --> 49:26.652
You... You said you lost earlier.

831
49:26.735 --> 49:28.112
What did you mean?

832
49:29.238 --> 49:31.991
What did you mean by that? Huh?

833
49:34.577 --> 49:35.578
[car honks]

834
50:06.483 --> 50:07.484
[door lock chimes]

835
50:14.325 --> 50:15.326
[door lock beeps]

836
50:57.576 --> 50:59.578
[cellphone vibrating]

837
51:17.638 --> 51:19.640
[line ringing]

838
51:23.811 --> 51:24.937
[automation] The phone is turned off.

839
51:25.020 --> 51:26.814
You will now be connected to voicemail.

840
51:26.897 --> 51:28.524
You will be charged after the tone.

841
51:31.110 --> 51:33.112
-[line disconnects] -[♪ music fades]

842
52:07.604 --> 52:08.605
Minjae.

843
52:08.689 --> 52:09.690
[Minjae] Yeah?

844
52:09.773 --> 52:12.067
Professor Ahn wants you in his office.

845
52:12.151 --> 52:15.028
But he seems a little... upset.

846
52:16.196 --> 52:18.198
Oh. Right, okay.

847
52:19.658 --> 52:20.659
[Taeho] Okay.

848
52:25.038 --> 52:27.207
What's up? Did something bad happen?

849
52:27.708 --> 52:29.084
[Taeho] Ah. Well, no. Nothing bad...

850
52:31.545 --> 52:33.172
[sighs] Is it bad?

851
52:34.089 --> 52:35.090
[Chansoo] What?

852
52:35.674 --> 52:38.218
[Taeho] There was a postdoc position in the States,

853
52:38.302 --> 52:39.636
but Minjae turned it down.

854
52:40.387 --> 52:42.264
-[Hangyeol] What? -[Chansoo] Minjae did his PhD in Korea,

855
52:42.347 --> 52:43.682
so he needs a postdoc abroad.

856
52:44.308 --> 52:45.517
[sighs]

857
52:45.601 --> 52:48.312
Well, he could go into industry.

858
52:48.395 --> 52:50.397
It looked like he had other plans in mind.

859
52:56.069 --> 52:59.114
Well, they asked you about your schedule,

860
53:00.824 --> 53:03.160
so I told them you're done with your dissertation

861
53:03.243 --> 53:05.162
and just need to wrap things up

862
53:06.163 --> 53:07.414
and defend it.

863
53:07.498 --> 53:08.665
[Minjae] Yes.

864
53:08.749 --> 53:10.250
Everything just fell into place.

865
53:10.334 --> 53:12.002
Why did you turn it down?

866
53:12.795 --> 53:13.796
Well...

867
53:14.630 --> 53:16.507
I don't think I'm ready yet.

868
53:16.590 --> 53:18.217
Ready for what?

869
53:18.300 --> 53:20.010
All you had to do was go.

870
53:22.137 --> 53:24.139
It's a rare opportunity, you know.

871
53:24.765 --> 53:25.766
But

872
53:26.558 --> 53:28.352
I could do a postdoc here, too.

873
53:29.061 --> 53:32.606
And getting a job at a research institute in Korea wouldn't be bad either.

874
53:32.689 --> 53:35.776
You said you eventually wanted to teach at a university.

875
53:36.693 --> 53:38.612
Now you're getting a research job in Korea?

876
53:39.613 --> 53:43.283
I'm thinking maybe getting a job wouldn't be so bad.

877
53:43.909 --> 53:45.160
Is there...

878
53:46.203 --> 53:48.664
something going on that I don't know about?

879
53:48.747 --> 53:49.748
What?

880
53:49.832 --> 53:52.960
[Jaehong] I heard you had a rough time when your leg got inflamed before.

881
53:53.043 --> 53:54.920
Is something wrong with your health?

882
53:56.296 --> 53:58.590
[Minjae] No, that's not what this is about.

883
53:59.675 --> 54:01.426
I just... I just want

884
54:01.885 --> 54:03.679
to keep my options open.

885
54:07.558 --> 54:09.685
Why do you think he suddenly decided not to go?

886
54:12.396 --> 54:13.605
Did something happen?

887
54:14.648 --> 54:16.775
Does he want to go to a different country?

888
54:17.568 --> 54:18.777
What do you think it is?

889
54:19.486 --> 54:20.821
[Jihoon] Go ask him yourself.

890
54:22.614 --> 54:23.740
I can't right now.

891
54:23.824 --> 54:25.158
Things are a little tense.

892
54:25.242 --> 54:26.660
[Jihoon] Isn't it actually a good thing?

893
54:27.828 --> 54:28.829
What?

894
54:29.538 --> 54:32.583
[Jihoon] It's "out of sight, out of mind," as they say.

895
54:32.666 --> 54:34.960
You'd rather have him close than be apart, right?

896
54:37.045 --> 54:38.589
Yeah, I would.

897
54:38.672 --> 54:40.257
I would, but still...

898
54:43.051 --> 54:45.971
There's no way he decided not to go because of me, right?

899
54:46.805 --> 54:48.098
[Jihoon] Would you like it if he did?

900
54:48.640 --> 54:49.850
No.

901
54:49.933 --> 54:51.059
[Jihoon] Why not?

902
54:51.143 --> 54:53.145
He's giving up on his dream for you.

903
54:53.228 --> 54:54.896
That shows how much he loves you.

904
54:57.566 --> 54:59.401
What if he regrets it later?

905
55:01.653 --> 55:05.782
He could regret giving up on his dream because of me and resent me for it.

906
55:05.866 --> 55:07.743
Then that's just how small a man he is.

907
55:07.826 --> 55:09.536
And that's just how much he cared.

908
55:16.793 --> 55:17.794
What?

909
55:18.837 --> 55:20.672
You have a weird habit, you know.

910
55:21.632 --> 55:23.508
What habit? I don't have any habits.

911
55:23.592 --> 55:24.593
You do.

912
55:24.676 --> 55:26.428
You try to do other people's homework.

913
55:27.220 --> 55:29.640
Why do you keep trying to make his decisions for him?

914
55:30.849 --> 55:34.102
He gets to make his own decisions, and he's responsible for them.

915
55:34.186 --> 55:37.397
You just look at your own feelings, and make your own decisions.

916
55:37.481 --> 55:38.565
Do your own homework.

917
55:41.860 --> 55:44.780
I can't tell if you get it or if you're just nodding along.

918
55:45.489 --> 55:46.490
I got it.

919
55:46.573 --> 55:47.574
[Jihoon] No, you didn't.

920
55:48.283 --> 55:51.536
And hey, you should say all this to him, not me.

921
55:51.620 --> 55:52.788
Talk to him directly.

922
55:52.871 --> 55:55.040
Why do you bring your drama to me? I'm busy.

923
55:56.667 --> 55:58.126
You always find it entertaining.

924
55:58.210 --> 55:59.753
Entertaining, my ass. Now go.

925
56:17.771 --> 56:20.148
[door bell chimes]

926
56:30.117 --> 56:31.118
[Minjae grunts softly]

927
56:32.619 --> 56:33.620
[Youjin] You're late.

928
56:35.122 --> 56:36.123
I'm right on time.

929
56:37.124 --> 56:38.291
[Youjin] But I got here earlier.

930
56:43.130 --> 56:44.923
Right. You should order a drink.

931
56:45.006 --> 56:46.049
[Minjae] I'm good.

932
56:46.133 --> 56:47.634
I need to head back soon anyway.

933
56:48.927 --> 56:50.178
Why did you want to see me?

934
56:52.222 --> 56:54.182
I had something to ask you...

935
56:56.309 --> 56:57.853
about your postdoc in the States.

936
56:57.936 --> 56:59.730
[Minjae] Let me ask you something first.

937
57:00.689 --> 57:02.607
When you said you lost, what did you mean?

938
57:03.358 --> 57:04.359
[Youjin] What?

939
57:04.443 --> 57:07.028
You said that it really sucks and that you lost.

940
57:08.155 --> 57:09.489
What did you mean by that?

941
57:11.658 --> 57:13.660
[mumbling] When I said that...

942
57:16.371 --> 57:18.039
I was really upset,

943
57:18.123 --> 57:19.499
so I can't really remember.

944
57:21.168 --> 57:22.335
You can't remember?

945
57:22.836 --> 57:25.088
I mean, I don't remember the exact words,

946
57:25.839 --> 57:26.923
but I kind of remember.

947
57:27.007 --> 57:28.049
So tell me.

948
57:28.133 --> 57:29.342
What did you mean?

949
57:32.512 --> 57:34.181
It meant I was really upset.

950
57:36.391 --> 57:37.601
"I lose.

951
57:37.684 --> 57:38.769
"You win.

952
57:39.269 --> 57:40.395
"Good for you.

953
57:40.479 --> 57:42.105
"You're so great."

954
57:42.189 --> 57:43.273
That's what it means.

955
57:48.361 --> 57:50.071
Did it mean anything else?

956
57:51.281 --> 57:52.282
What?

957
57:54.451 --> 57:55.452
So...

958
57:56.787 --> 57:58.163
you didn't mean

959
57:59.873 --> 58:02.000
you wanted to break up, or stop seeing me?

960
58:02.584 --> 58:03.919
That's not what I meant.

961
58:07.130 --> 58:08.131
[chuckles softly]

962
58:09.049 --> 58:11.301
I mean, couples fight sometimes.

963
58:12.260 --> 58:14.179
Do we have to break up every time we fight?

964
58:15.514 --> 58:16.807
No, of course not.

965
58:18.975 --> 58:20.602
[inhales sharply] Minjae,

966
58:21.269 --> 58:23.188
have you really never dated before?

967
58:23.271 --> 58:24.272
[chuckling] What?

968
58:28.235 --> 58:29.903
Well, actually, more importantly,

969
58:31.196 --> 58:34.199
what happened with that postdoc in the States?

970
58:34.282 --> 58:35.408
Oh, that.

971
58:36.618 --> 58:38.411
I don't need to go.

972
58:41.540 --> 58:44.417
Is it... because of me?

973
58:45.502 --> 58:47.087
[inhales]

974
58:48.505 --> 58:49.589
I'm fine with it.

975
58:50.715 --> 58:52.717
I told you, I can wait a year or so.

976
58:53.260 --> 58:54.386
I'm not fine with it.

977
58:54.469 --> 58:56.054
I don't want to be away from you.

978
58:57.806 --> 58:59.766
[Youjin] I can't go to the States, though.

979
58:59.850 --> 59:01.101
That's why I'm not going.

980
59:03.603 --> 59:04.771
I just...

981
59:06.398 --> 59:07.983
want to do my best for you.

982
59:11.820 --> 59:14.322
How is giving up on your dreams doing your best?

983
59:18.159 --> 59:21.663
You don't have to choose between your dream and love.

984
59:25.792 --> 59:26.793
It's only a year.

985
59:28.587 --> 59:30.422
We'll be together again next spring.

986
59:30.505 --> 59:32.507
[♪ gentle music playing]

987
59:33.758 --> 59:34.926
I'll be right here,

988
59:36.011 --> 59:38.138
and I'll be an even better person by then.

989
01:00:45.622 --> 01:00:47.666
I'VE BEEN DYING TO SEE YOU!

990
01:00:47.749 --> 01:00:49.751
WELCOME

991
01:00:56.424 --> 01:00:57.425
[Youjin chuckles]

992
01:00:58.468 --> 01:01:00.470
[♪ dramatic Italian ballad playing]

993
01:01:39.634 --> 01:01:43.555
BETWEEN STEPS

994
01:01:43.638 --> 01:01:45.974
[Subin] Is Youjin seeing someone?

995
01:01:46.057 --> 01:01:48.309
Because I missed you so much.

996
01:01:48.393 --> 01:01:50.103
I met Park Minjae there.

997
01:01:50.186 --> 01:01:52.772
[Youjin] I pray that the woman he likes brutally dumps him

998
01:01:52.856 --> 01:01:54.149
and leaves him in tears.

999
01:01:54.232 --> 01:01:56.443
[Hangyeol] Minjae's coming back to Korea after his postdoc.

1000
01:01:56.818 --> 01:02:00.155
Did you tell Minjae to break up with Youjin?

1001
01:02:00.238 --> 01:02:01.489
[glass clatters]

1002
01:02:02.032 --> 01:02:05.702
[Minjae] If there's anything on your mind, let it all out.

1003
01:02:07.787 --> 01:02:09.205
You're making the right choice.
